<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Asbestos disposal in Geelong is narrower than most people expect. EPA Victoria keeps a register of landfills licensed to receive asbestos waste, and across Greater Geelong, the Bellarine, the Surf Coast and Golden Plains there is exactly one site on it: Drysdale Landfill, run by the City of Greater Geelong. Every other tip and transfer station in the region is closed to it.</p><p>That one fact decides most of what follows. Asbestos waste is pre-classified as reportable priority waste in Victoria, so it has to be wrapped, labelled and taken to an authorised landfill, and it can never go in a general skip or out with a council hard waste collection. If you are not certain the sheeting is asbestos at all, <a href="/asbestos-testing-geelong/">get it tested before you touch it</a>. A lab result costs a lot less than a wasted trip to the tip.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">One licensed site in the region</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">EPA Victoria's register, Landfills licensed for asbestos waste, was updated 22 June 2026 and lists 26 sites statewide. Only one of them is in the Barwon region: Drysdale Landfill, licence OL000072476.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Ring before you load the trailer</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">EPA's advice is to contact the landfill before you transport and deliver, because a licensed site can still choose not to accept a load and may want you booked in. Drysdale's number is (03) 5251 2935.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Small domestic loads only</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Drysdale takes small domestic quantities, capped at a 6x4 trailer. Bigger loads and trade quantities are a different conversation, and they sit with a licensed removalist who holds the EPA transport permission.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Wrapped in 200 micron polythene</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Sheeting goes in polythene about 200 micron (0.2 mm) thick, sealed with adhesive tape. Dust and friable material go into double bags of the same thickness, filled half full, with a loaded weight no more than 30 kg.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Labelled before it moves</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Every package carries the asbestos warning mark, roughly 75 mm by 90 mm, reading CAUTION ASBESTOS DO NOT OPEN OR DAMAGE BAG DO NOT INHALE DUST. All containers have to display it before transport starts.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">An asbestos bin is its own product</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The bin is lined and taped, the waste is bagged before it goes in, and the price is a hire fee plus a separate tipping fee charged by weight. A general waste skip cannot take asbestos at any price.</p>
      </div>
</div>
